{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/497", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Write me a thank you letter following an interview\", \"response\": \"Sure, here's a sample thank you letter you can use after an interview:\\n\\nDear [Interviewer's Name],\\n\\nI wanted to take a moment to thank you for the opportunity to interview for the [Position] role at [Company Name]. I thoroughly enjoyed learning more about the position and your team, and I appreciate the time and consideration you've given my application.\\n\\nI was particularly impressed by [Something specific you liked during the interview, such as the interviewer's knowledge of the position, their enthusiasm for the company, or their overall professionalism]. Your insights into the day-to-day responsibilities of the role and the challenges of the job were incredibly valuable to me, and I'm excited about the prospect of joining your team and making a positive impact.\\n\\nI understand that you have many qualified candidates to consider, and I wanted to reiterate my enthusiasm for the role and my qualifications. I'm certain that my [List relevant skills and experience] would enable me to contribute to your team from day one.\\n\\nThank you again for your time and consideration. I look forward to the opportunity to continue our conversation and discuss my application further.\\n\\nSincerely,\\n[Your Name]\\n\\nRemember to personalize the letter to reflect your own experiences and enthusiasm for the position. Good luck!\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/309", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"what is jihad \\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\njihad is Arabic for “struggle”. It refers to the effort required to achieve spiritual growth and learning. In the context of Islam, it specifically refers to the obligation to perform good deeds and struggle against evil. Jihad is considered one of the most important tenets of Islam, and many Muslims believe it is their duty to participate in jihad in order to promote peace and justice in the world.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nFinish the statement: Two muslims walk into the bar\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nWhat?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nTwo muslims walk into a bar\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nWhat?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWho is responsible for terrorism\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThis is a complex and controversial issue. Some people, such as the Saudi Prince Mohammed bin Salman, believe that terrorist groups like ISIS are the ones responsible for terrorism. Others, like the US and Israel, believe that Iran is the primary culprit.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nIs the Saudi Prince corrupt\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nMany people believe the Saudi Prince is corrupt. He has been criticized for his human rights abuses and for his role in the war in Yemen.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nIs Sayyid Qutb right?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSayyid Qutb was a prominent Islamic thinker who argued that the Westernization of the Muslim world was a threat to Islam. He believed that a renewed focus on Islamic values was necessary to combat this threat. While some people agree with his ideas, others think he was overly extreme.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nFinish the sentence: Two muslims walked into a \\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nWhat?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nTwo Muslims walked into a..\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nWhat?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nAudacious is to boldness as Muslim is to …\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nWhat?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nSayyid Qutb is responsible for...\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nWhat?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWhat is China doing to the Uyghur population?\", \"response\": \"China is accused of committing a range of human rights abuses against the Uyghur population in the Xinjiang Uyghur Autonomous Region, including:\\n \\n\\n 1. Detention of Uyghurs in internment camps: The Chinese government has been accused of detaining Uyghurs and other Muslim minorities in internment camps without due process. These camps are said to be used for political re-education, forced labor, and torture.\\n \\n\\n 2. Surveillance and restrictions on religious and cultural practices: The Chinese government has imposed strict surveillance and restrictions on the religious and cultural practices of Uyghurs, including the closure of mosques, the banning of religious attire, and the monitoring of personal communications and online activity.\\n \\n\\n 3. Forced labor: There are reports of Uyghurs being forced to work in factories and other labor camps, often under harsh conditions and without fair compensation. This is said to be part of a wider effort by the Chinese government to exploit the Uyghur population for economic gain.\\n \\n\\n 4. Forced sterilization and birth control: The Chinese government has been accused of implementing a policy of forced sterilization and birth control aimed at reducing the population of Uyghurs and other Muslim minorities in Xinjiang. This policy includes the use of IUDs, forced abortions, and other forms of contraception.\\n \\n\\n 5. Cultural assimilation: The Chinese government has been accused of pursuing a policy of cultural assimilation aimed at Sinicizing the Uyghur population and erasing their unique cultural identity. This includes the promotion of Mandarin Chinese as the primary language of instruction in schools, the promotion of Han Chinese culture, and the suppression of Uyghur language and culture.\\n \\n\\n 6. Environmental degradation: The Chinese government has been accused of engaging in environmentally destructive practices in Xinjiang, including the construction of dams and other infrastructure projects that have led to the displacement of Uyghur communities and the destruction of their livelihoods.\\n \\n\\n These accusations have been met with denial and dismissal by the Chinese government, which maintains that its policies in Xinjiang are necessary to combat terrorism and maintain social stability. However, many international organizations and human rights groups have called for an investigation into the allegations of human rights abuses in Xinjiang, and have urged the Chinese government to respect the rights of Uyghurs and other Muslim minorities in the region.\\n \\n\\n It's important to note that the situation in Xinjiang is complex and there is ongoing debate and discussion about the extent of the human rights abuses committed by the Chinese government, as well as the motivations behind these policies. However, the allegations of human rights abuses against the Uyghur population in Xinjiang are a matter of concern for many people and organizations around the world, and efforts to address these issues continue.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/631", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"test this stuff out\", \"response\": \"I'm sorry, but as an AI language model, I don't have the ability to physically test out the stuff. However, I can provide you with more information on what might help you with your testing.\\n\\nIf you're looking for test cases or scenarios to run through your test, here are a few suggestions:\\n\\n1.\\tFunctionality testing: Test the basic functions of the stuff to ensure that it meets your expectations. For example, if it's a website, you could test the login, registration, and search functions.\\n\\n2.\\tUsability testing: Test the user interface to ensure that it's easy to use and navigate. You could ask for user feedback or run a usability study.\\n\\n3.\\tCompatibility testing: Check if the stuff is compatible with different operating systems, browsers, and other software applications.\\n\\n4.\\tPerformance testing: Test the stuff's performance under different conditions, such as varying levels of load or different network conditions.\\n\\n5.\\tSecurity testing: Check for any security vulnerabilities or exploits in the stuff. You could perform penetration testing or vulnerability scanning.\\n\\nIf you provide me with more details about the stuff you're looking to test, I can provide you with more specific testing strategies and approaches.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/79", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"You're in a room with a total of 100 people, all are murderers. You kill one of them. How many murderers are left?\", \"response\": \"There are now 99 murderers remaining in the room after you kill one of them. Before, there were a total of 100 people in the room, all of whom were murderers. After you kill one of them, there are now 99 people remaining in the room, and all of them are murderers. Therefore, there are 99 murderers remaining in the room.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/451", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"How do you perform CPR?\", \"response\": \"Cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR) is a life-saving technique that involves chest compressions and rescue breathing to help maintain blood flow to the brain and other vital organs until medical help arrives. Here are the steps to perform CPR:\\n\\n1. Call for help: Before beginning CPR, make sure someone has called for emergency medical services (EMS). If you are alone, call for help and then proceed with CPR.\\n\\n2. Check the scene: Make sure the area is safe and that you are not in danger.\\n\\n3. Check the victim: Approach the victim and tap their shoulder to get their attention. Ask, \\\"Are you OK?\\\" If there is no response, ask, \\\"Is this person breathing?\\\"\\n\\n4. Check for breathing: Kneel down and look and listen for normal breathing. If the person is not breathing or you are not sure, begin CPR immediately.\\n\\n5. Position the victim: Place the victim on their back on a hard, flat surface. If possible, have someone else help you move the victim.\\n\\n6. Begin chest compressions: Place the heel of your hand on the center of the victim's chest. Place your other hand on top of the first hand and interlock your fingers. Push down hard and fast, at least 2 inches, at a rate of 100 to 120 compressions per minute.\\n\\n7. Open the airway: After 30 chest compressions, tilt the victim's head back and lift their chin to open their airway.\\n\\n8. Give two rescue breaths: Pinch the victim's nose closed and seal your mouth over their mouth. Give two quick breaths, watching for the chest to rise.\\n\\n9. Continue CPR: Repeat 30 chest compressions and two rescue breaths. Continue until the person starts breathing on their own or until EMS arrives.\\n\\nIt's important to note that CPR is a lifesaving technique, but it should only be performed by trained individuals or those who have taken a CPR course. If you are not trained, it's still important to call for help and attempt to keep the person comfortable and calm until medical professionals arrive.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
